1) Product of an orderly mind, I'm a computer
programmer by profession.

2) Pets, and perhaps monsters, have a nasty habit of
carrying boxes and chests, even between levels off
and on (trapdoor, for example), so the label is more
a "where I want it" label than a "where it is"
label.

Once I put enough junk into boxes to make them
unweildy, and I deliberately fatten them with rocks
for this reason, they don't tend to be carted around
as much, but to start with, it's a good idea to know
where it is supposed to be, when I next encounter it
where it in fact is.

After a while, I can E-word the spot it sits,
dropped something cursed on top, and otherwise make
it unattractive, but I don't have all those
resources, early on, and with my playing skills,
"early on" is pretty much as long as most of my
games last anyway.

